# Instagram archive

Continuously dump `@efemer_flowers` and `@himmlhaus` into `posts` (idempotent on `instagramAccount` + `instagramShortcode`).

## Session

Store Jan’s Instagram `sessionid` in Secret Manager (never commit it):

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Project | `efemer-456414` |
| Secret | `instagram-session-id` |
| Accessor | `efemer-storage@efemer-456414.iam.gserviceaccount.com` |

Runtime reads GSM first, then `.secret/instagram.session`. Local file is seeded into GSM when GSM is empty.

Refresh the secret when Instagram checkpoints the session:

```bash
printf '%s' "$SESSIONID" | gcloud secrets versions add instagram-session-id \
  --project=efemer-456414 --account=jablunka@gmail.com --data-file=-
```

## Run

```bash
docker compose exec -T php php bin/archive-instagram.php
docker compose exec -T php php bin/archive-instagram.php --full
```

Production `instagram-archive` service loops every 6 hours. Each run imports up to 20 new posts per account, skips shortcodes already in the database, then walks older posts until the profile is backfilled.

`@himmlhaus` → Himmelhaus. `@efemer_flowers` classified by caption. Confidence below 0.75 → status `review`.
